  <ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock id="f-57" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-left:13.5pt;text-indent:-13.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:5.17pt"&gt;OVERHEAD:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Administrative, engineering, and supervision salaries, expenses, and employee benefits relating to construction activities are capitalized based on labor recorded to the payroll system. The amounts so capitalized are directly assigned, based on individual construction projects. Employees charge their time and expenses directly to individual construction projects by each hour worked as assigned. Employee benefits are derived based on the labor hours charged to each individual project.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2. ALLOWANCE FOR FUNDS USED DURING CONSTRUCTION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Computed monthly on construction work in progress, exclusive of construction projects covering the purchase of property normally placed in service when received. The amounts so capitalized are directly charged, based on individual construction projects exclusive of capital spares and construction orders covering the purchase of general plant furniture, transportation equipment, tools and similar property.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:GeneralDescriptionOfConstructionOverheadTextBlock>
